# Whisper Desktop (Dark-Whisper) - Project Memory

## Project Overview
**Whisper Desktop** is a Windows desktop app (Electron) that records audio on a global hotkey, transcribes it, and pastes the text into the active window. Transcription runs on a **bundled whisper.cpp server** by default; an external Whisper-compatible API (OpenAI or self-hosted) is also supported.

Repository: https://github.com/TheGeek01/Dark-Whisper (fork of dniasoff/whisper-desktop). Current version: 1.1.0.

### Key Features
- Global hotkey (default `Ctrl+Q`): press to start, press again to stop; 5-minute cap
- Built-in whisper.cpp server, supervised by the app (start, health-check, restart, stop)
- Speech model manager: curated Hugging Face GGML models pinned by SHA256, plus custom model URLs
- GPU acceleration via Vulkan with automatic CPU fallback; "Force CPU" setting
- Auto-paste with clipboard preservation; auto-mute of system audio while recording
- Tray icon with status tooltip, Show/Hide, Models…, Exit
- Auto-start on Windows login; recordings auto-deleted after 7 days

## Technical Stack
- **Framework**: Electron 44.4.0
- **Language**: TypeScript 6.0.3 (`module: node20`, CommonJS output)
- **Transcription**: whisper.cpp `b5130` (tag pinned in `whisper.version`), CPU + Vulkan builds
- **Audio**: node-mic 1.0.1 (bundles sox.exe; 16 kHz mono WAV)
- **Keystrokes**: @nut-tree-fork/libnut 4.2.6 (`keyTap('v', 'control')`)
- **HTTP**: axios 1.20.0 | **Settings**: electron-store 11.0.2 | **Multipart**: form-data 4.0.6
- **Build**: electron-builder 26.15.3 (config only in `electron-builder.yml`)
- **Tests**: Jest 30.5.1 + ts-jest — 123 tests, 11 suites | **Lint**: ESLint 10

## Architecture
Logic lives in Electron-free modules; one wiring module touches Electron. Jest cannot load Electron, so tests must never import `electron`, `electron-store`, `settingsService`, `whisperRuntime` or `main`.

- **main.ts** — window, tray, hotkey, lifecycle, all IPC handlers, recording gate
- **preload.ts** — `contextBridge` API; type-only imports so the bundle requires only `electron`
- **public/index.html** — vanilla JS UI: status line, setup banner, settings modal, models modal; dynamic text via `textContent` only

Electron-free services (unit-tested): `modelCatalog`, `modelManager`, `whisperServer`, `serverOutput`, `serverPaths`, `serverGate`, `settingsMigration`.
Electron-bound services: `whisperRuntime` (spawn, ports, `/health`, PID file, log file, stale cleanup), `settingsService`, `apiService`, `recordingService`, `audioControlService`, `pasteService`, `hotkeyService`.

## Transcription API (same for built-in and external)
- `GET /health` (built-in) or `GET /v1/health` (external) — readiness
- `POST /v1/audio/transcriptions` — multipart `file`, returns `{ "text": ... }`
- Timeouts: built-in 300 000 ms, external 30 000 ms

## Server Lifecycle (whisperServer.ts)
States: `no-model` | `starting` | `ready` | `error` | `stopped`.
- Args: `-m <model file name> --host 127.0.0.1 --port <free port> --inference-path /v1/audio/transcriptions`, spawned with `cwd` = the model's directory. **The relative `-m` plus `cwd` is deliberate**: whisper-server reads argv as ANSI but decodes the path as UTF-8, so absolute paths break on non-ASCII profiles (e.g. `C:\Users\José`).
- Readiness: poll `/health` every 500 ms up to 120 s (the model loads before the port opens).
- GPU label comes from the server log (`whisper_backend_init_gpu: using … backend` vs `no GPU found`), not from the chosen binary.
- Vulkan process exiting before readiness (without a model-load error) → retry on CPU and remember per version. Model-load failure → error, no fallback.
- Crash restarts: 1 s, 5 s, 15 s, then error; counter resets after 5 min healthy.
- Every launch bumps a generation counter; stale callbacks are ignored.
- PID written to `userData/whisper-server.pid`; a stale process is killed only if its image is `whisper-server.exe`.
- Binary resolution: `WHISPER_SERVER_DIR` (Vulkan, dev only) → `process.resourcesPath/whisper/<backend>/` when packaged → `<repo>/resources/whisper/<backend>/` in dev. Version read from `whisper/VERSION`.

## Model Handling (modelCatalog.ts / modelManager.ts)
- Curated list pinned to size + SHA256; recommended model `ggml-large-v3-turbo-q5_0.bin` (547 MB).
- Custom URLs must match `https://huggingface.co/<owner>/<repo>/resolve/<rev>/<file>.bin`; id is `custom/<owner>__<repo>__<file>`; SHA256 read from `X-Linked-ETag` on Hugging Face's 302 (no-redirect HEAD first).
- Download to `<file>.part`, verify SHA256 + GGML magic (`readUInt32LE(0) === 0x67676d6c`), then rename. One download at a time; progress throttled to 250 ms; stray `.part` files swept at startup.

## Settings (electron-store, config.json)
`serverMode` (`builtin`/`external`), `modelId`, `forceCpu`, `gpuFallbackVersion`, `shortcut`, `micDevice`, `autoMuteAudio`, `apiUrl`, `apiToken`.
Migration: if `serverMode` is absent and `config.json` already existed → `external` (upgrades keep working); fresh installs → `builtin`. `serverMode` is deliberately NOT in electron-store defaults, or the migration check would never fire.

## Data Locations (`%APPDATA%\whisper-desktop\`)
`config.json`, `models\`, `recordings\`, `logs\whisper-server.log`, `whisper-server.pid`.

## CI / Release
`.github/workflows/publish.yml` on a `v*.*.*` tag: lint → test (Ubuntu) → build-whisper (Windows: pinned Vulkan SDK 1.4.357.0, compiles CPU + Vulkan `whisper-server` from `whisper.version`, smoke-tests a real transcription, caches per version) → build-and-release (downloads the artifact to `resources/whisper/`, builds NSIS, publishes a Release).

## Development Notes
- Re-check `serverOutput.classifyServerLine` strings when bumping `whisper.version`.
- Electron 44 clipboard calls are async — always await them.
- In Git Bash, prefix manual server commands with `MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1`, or `/v1/...` args get rewritten into Windows paths.
- Vulkan builds only come from CI; locally use `npm run whisper:fetch` (CPU) or `WHISPER_SERVER_DIR`.
- Tests use real temp directories and injected fakes; no real processes or network, so they pass on Ubuntu CI.
- Design spec and implementation plan: `docs/superpowers/`.
